# Rules that must travel with this directory.
#
# They are redundant inside the SDK checkout — its root .gitignore already covers all of it —
# and they are the whole protection once this becomes its own repository, where `api.conf`
# sits at the root and the SDK's `apps/telegram/api.conf` line no longer matches anything.
# Without this file, the first `git add -A` in the new repo commits live API credentials.

# Telegram application credentials, and the dev bridge's host address.
api.conf

# Build output: the staticlib, the objects, the E32 image, the package.
build/
**/target/

# Any E32 image, wherever it lands. `build/` above covers the ones symbuild writes, and this
# covers the ones that get copied out of it: a `telegram-0-e1234569.exe` sat in this root for
# 25 commits and had to be removed from the history, because api_id and api_hash arrive
# through `option_env!("TG_API_ID")` and are compiled into the image as plain literals.
# An .exe here is a credential file that does not look like one.
*.exe

# The application icon, regenerated from data/mkicon.py on every build. The generator
# is the source that can be reviewed; these are two binaries that cannot. Committing
# them would also mean a rebuild dirties the tree on a machine that changed nothing.
data/*_icon.bmp
data/*_icon_mask.bmp

# The raw 2x output of `cargo run --example preview`, ~900 KB a sheet because the PNG
# writer uses stored deflate blocks. The curated set under docs/screenshots/ is the same
# pixels re-encoded with a palette - 6 screens in 69 KB - and that one is committed.
preview-out/
